WEBVTT

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:05.657
With proxymock connected, your coding agent
can record a local service and replay that

00:00:05.657 --> 00:00:07.843
traffic with recorded dependencies.

00:00:08.014 --> 00:00:09.791
We'll use the mock-lab orders app.

00:00:10.352 --> 00:00:15.441
Once the tutorial app is set up, ask the
agent to use the record traffic skill while

00:00:15.441 --> 00:00:16.895
the traffic driver runs.

00:00:17.066 --> 00:00:21.435
Include the app's database calls and its C
N C F API calls.

00:00:21.985 --> 00:00:24.026
Open one of the recorded requests.

00:00:24.197 --> 00:00:27.873
Here, a post to /orders returned two oh one
created.

00:00:28.044 --> 00:00:32.269
The corresponding outbound calls were
captured in separate host folders.

00:00:32.819 --> 00:00:38.146
Follow the tutorial's tuning chapters, then
ask the agent to start the mocks and run a

00:00:38.146 --> 00:00:40.809
local replay with the tutorial test config.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.753
Ask it to report assertion results and mock
matches separately.

00:00:45.319 --> 00:00:50.753
In this recorded tutorial run, four hundred
and five assertions passed across a hundred

00:00:50.753 --> 00:00:52.877
and thirty-five replayed requests.

00:00:53.048 --> 00:00:55.391
The mock report also shows that all

00:00:55.391 --> 00:00:58.805
observed outbound calls matched recorded
responses.

00:00:59.352 --> 00:01:03.351
Follow the same loop after a code change
and compare the next result.
